      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While coincidences can feel highly significant, the frequency and specific timing of these events often point toward cognitive shifts, such as hyper-awareness or a stress-induced narrowing of attention, rather than an actual physical force. When people are in high emotional distress, they may become acutely sensitive to environmental changes or recall events too narrowly, making random occurrences seem perfectly choreographed around their feelings. To regain control and safety, focusing on developing coping strategies for your emotions and considering a consultation with a mental health professional is a much more practical and effective path forward.",
